o:CL_0000344 (obsolete non-visual cell (sensu Vertebrata))\n\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000344 \"obsolete non-visual cell (sensu Vertebrata)\")\nAnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000344 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0000345 (dental papilla cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000345 \"A mesenchymal cell that is part of a small mass of condensed mesenchyme in the enamel organ; it differentiates into the dentin and dental pulp.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000345 \"Merge with odontoblast?\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000345 \"dental papilla cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000345 obo:CL_0008019)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000345 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001763))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000345 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000008))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0000346 (hair follicle dermal papilla cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28418596\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39798934\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40867641\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000346 \"A specialized fibroblast that resides in the dermal papilla located at the bottom of hair follicles. This cell orchestrates reciprocal epithelial-mesenchymal signaling essential for hair follicle morphogenesis and cycling, regulating matrix cell proliferation and differentiation to control hair shaft size, shape, and growth. The dermal papilla cell is replenished each hair cycle from bipotent hair follicle dermal stem cells in the dermal sheath that simultaneously self-renew and contribute progeny to the papilla, particularly during anagen.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39798934\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000346 \"hair follicle DPC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21444748\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000346 \"The dermal papilla contains functionally heterogeneous Sox2-positive subpopulations that serve as a niche for multipotent stem cells. These cells exhibit progenitor properties, generate skin-derived precursors (SKPs), and can differentiate into adipogenic and osteogenic lineages.\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
